Ladybird lays out and repaints an SVG image again when a web font its
document uses finishes loading. The other engines do too: In Blink,
RemoteFontFaceSource::NotifyFinished() invalidates the image document’s
font selector, and SVGImageChromeClient::InvalidateContainer() tells the
image’s observers. In WebKit, CSSFontSelector::fontLoaded() starts the
document’s font update. And in Gecko, UserFontSetUpdated() dirties the
frames using the font, which VectorImage reports to its observers.
